//Parameterized Constructor

A parameterized constructor is a constructor that takes one or more parameters.

Example:

class Student {
public:
    string name;
    int age;

    Student(string n, int a) {
        name = n;
        age = a;
    }
};

Now when creating an object, we provide the values:

Student s1("Shubham", 20);
Student s2("Rahul", 21);

So:

s1.name → "Shubham"
s1.age → 20
s2.name → "Rahul"
s2.age → 21
Why use it?

It allows us to initialize different objects with different values at the time of creation.

Compare:

Default constructor:

Student s1;

Parameterized constructor:

Student s1("Shubham", 20);

Simple definition:

Parameterized constructor = constructor that accepts parameters to initialize an object with specific values.